sections.text:
As used in this Ordinance, the following terms shall mean:

(a) Electric Bicycle (E-Bike) - refers to any two- or three-wheeled vehicle equipped with an electric motor and functional pedals;

(b) Electric Scooter (E-Scooter) - refers to a stand-up or sit-down light two-wheeled vehicle powered by an electric motor;

(c) City Streets - refers to roads and streets within Davao City not designated as national or provincial highways;

(d) Dedicated Bicycle Lanes - refers to designated lanes on public roads reserved for bicycles and light mobility conveyances;

(e) CTTMO - refers to the City Transport and Traffic Management Office of Davao City.

All riders and operators of electric bicycles and e-scooters traversing public roads in Davao City shall observe the following safety requirements:

(a) Mandatory wearing of protective bicycle or motorcycle safety helmets at all times;

(b) Equipping vehicles with operational white front headlights and red rear reflectors or tail lights during nighttime operation from 6:00 PM to 6:00 AM;

(c) Installation of functional mechanical brakes and an audible bell or horn;

(d) Prohibition against carrying passengers beyond the designed manufacturer capacity of the vehicle.

Any person issued a citation ticket for violation of Section 5 or Section 7 who does not wish to contest the citation may avail of the No-Contest provision by paying an administrative fine to the City Treasurer within seventy-two (72) hours:

(a) First Offense: Three Hundred Pesos (Php 300.00);

(b) Second Offense: Five Hundred Pesos (Php 500.00);

(c) Third Offense: One Thousand Pesos (Php 1,000.00).
